INT. RIVERSIDE SOUND STUDIO - CONTROL ROOM - NIGHT

A dim room, all faders and foam. Through the glass: a vocal booth, a lone mic, a stool.

ELLIE (17, borrowed leather jacket two sizes too big) stands inside the booth with headphones clamped on, gripping the mic stand while RHYS (30s, producer, beanie, tea in a chipped mug) slumps behind the desk with his feet up, and a laptop on his knee pings and BUZZES every few seconds as GRAN's name flashes on its screen.

RHYS
(into talkback)
Again, Ellie. From the second verse.

ELLIE (V.O.)
(through speaker)
I've done it nine times, Rhys.

RHYS
Ten's a good number.

She sighs, the speaker crackling. Rhys's phone rings: GRAN. He answers, puts it on speaker.

GRAN (V.O.)
Rhys, love, is she there? She's not answering her mobile.

RHYS
She's singing, Gran. Can't be disturbed.

GRAN (V.O.)
Tell her the dinner's gone cold. Tell her I'm proud, and the dinner's gone cold.

Ellie hears it through the cans. Her hand goes to her mouth. Rhys mutes the line and presses talkback.

RHYS
Good. Hold that. Sing it like that.

She takes a breath. Closes her eyes. The red light flicks on.
